 Joining Collibra’s Public Sector team  
Make an impact at Collibra Public Sector by driving growth in US federal civilian agencies. This role will be responsible for selling Collibra's value and vision to prospects and existing customers, offering a complete solution that includes software, support and services. As part of our federal sales team, you will manage some of Collibra’s largest accounts. You will use your knowledge and skills in enterprise sales to establish trusted and credible relationships, build Collibra’s brand and awareness around our solutions, and serve as a data intelligence advisor throughout the customer journey. You will be actively involved in the entire sales cycle&nbsp; 
 Senior Account Executives at Collibra Public Sector are responsible for  

Achieving assigned goals for new license revenue and customer renewals&nbsp;&nbsp; 
Reliable and accurate forecasting produced by high activity levels and broad account coverage&nbsp;&nbsp; 
Prospecting for net new accounts, building pipeline, expanding existing accounts, and developing relationships to maintain sufficient active deal pipeline&nbsp;&nbsp; 
Managing complex deal cycles, from lead origination to stakeholder mapping, through negotiation to close and expansion&nbsp;&nbsp; 
Successfully collaborating with customers, partners, and peers in a consultative sales process where you will identify value and ROI to support customer’s needs&nbsp; 

 You have  

Consistently exceeded assigned sales quotas&nbsp;&nbsp; 
Experience in the data storage or data management software industry&nbsp;&nbsp; 
7+ years experience calling on federal civilian accounts in a field sales capacity&nbsp;&nbsp; 
Prior relationships with Departments of Homeland Security and/or Department of Energy&nbsp; 
Originated and closed complex sales with multiple technical and business stakeholders 
Managed consultative sales processes, with value-based impacts or outcomes&nbsp;&nbsp; 
Demonstrated proficiency in leveraging AI tools (e.g., Claude, Gemini, ChatGPT, Copilot) to solve real-world business challenges, drive measurable outcomes, or streamline workflows 
A bachelor’s degree or equivalent related working experience is required 
Because this role supports the US government, it is required that this candidate be a US citizen who resides on US soil; Active security clearance (preferred)&nbsp; 

 You are  

Known for your integrity, and commitment to the customer&nbsp;&nbsp; 
Detail and results oriented – you work backwards from a goal using documented plans&nbsp; 
Composed, resourceful, and comfortable in high-growth high-expectation environments&nbsp; 
Adaptive, accountable, and execution-oriented&nbsp;&nbsp; 
A concise communicator, persuasive negotiator, collaborative seller&nbsp;&nbsp; 
Proud of your work and aim for excellence&nbsp;&nbsp; 
Flexible to travel as required&nbsp; 

