&lt;blockquote&gt;Are you deeply rooted in the Windows ecosystem?&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you a seasoned T-shaped engineer with a strong background in Windows, who understands the importance of automation? If you thrive on innovative problem-solving and thinking beyond the conventional, this opportunity might be perfect for you!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are seeking passionate Windows Automation Engineers focused on automation to join one of our self-steering customer teams. Here, you&#39;ll be part of a multi-disciplinary team of experts who get full responsibility for a customer environment to ensure our 100% customer satisfaction. We handle complex systems that are business-critical using the latest technologies. The team is responsible for the Plan, Build and Run phases of the environment and takes care of the full stack. Private cloud, operating systems, storage, networking, monitoring, automation, technical application management, security, compliancy – we handle it all in the team. No silos here!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;As a Windows Automation Engineer, you&#39;ll support the customer’s functional management team, ensuring their business satisfaction while continuously seeking improvements. You&#39;ll maintain platform security, ensure it is up-to-date and available, and engage in both critical operations and project work. Automation is key, so you’ll do a lot of configuration management in Chef, Infrastructure-as-code in Terraform and general scripting in PowerShell or Python (or anything else that makes sense!).&lt;/p&gt;
